---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const title = "Text Case Styles Explained: Title, Sentence, camelCase and More - Toolkit Lab";
const description = "A guide to text case styles: when to use Title Case or Sentence case in writing, and camelCase, snake_case or kebab-case in code.";
---
<Base title={title} description={description} path="/guides/text-case-styles-explained.html">
<aside class="ad-rail" aria-label="Advertisement"><div class="ad-slot ad-slot-rail"></div></aside>
    <div class="wrap article">
      <p class="note"><a href="/guides.html">Guides</a> / Text case</p>
      <h1>Text Case Styles Explained</h1>
      <p class="lead">Capitalization changes how a title or heading reads. In code, the case style also signals what a name means. Here is when to use each common style.</p>
      <div class="ad-slot" aria-label="Advertisement"></div>

      <h2>Writing styles</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>UPPERCASE</strong> is for short emphasis, acronyms and warning labels. Long passages in capitals are harder to read.</li>
        <li><strong>lowercase</strong> is often used in informal writing and in some brand names.</li>
        <li><strong>Title Case</strong> capitalizes most words in a headline. Style guides differ on which small words, such as "a", "of" and "the", stay lowercase. Pick one guide and be consistent.</li>
        <li><strong>Sentence case</strong> capitalizes only the first word and proper nouns. Many news sites and product interfaces use it because it is easier to read.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Code naming styles</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>camelCase</strong>: <code>userName</code>. Common for variables and functions in JavaScript and Java.</li>
        <li><strong>PascalCase</strong>: <code>UserName</code>. Common for classes and React components.</li>
        <li><strong>snake_case</strong>: <code>user_name</code>. Common in Python and in database column names.</li>
        <li><strong>kebab-case</strong>: <code>user-name</code>. Common in URLs, CSS class names and file names.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Watch out for the small details</h2>
      <p>Converting between styles can be tricky with acronyms and numbers. "XMLHttpRequest" becomes "xml_http_request" in snake_case, and "version 2 beta" becomes "version_2_beta". Always scan the result for words that split in unexpected places.</p>

      <h2>Try it yourself</h2>
      <p>Paste text into the <a href="../tools/case-converter.html">Case Converter</a> and click any style to see the result. You can then copy it or use it as the input for another conversion.</p>

      <!-- AdSense: place your ad unit code here once your site is approved. -->
      <div class="ad-slot" aria-label="Advertisement"></div>
    </div>
    <aside class="ad-rail" aria-label="Advertisement"><div class="ad-slot ad-slot-rail"></div></aside>

</Base>
